WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.157 --> 00:00:02.282
- It takes courage to win!

00:00:02.282 --> 00:00:04.597
People don't talk about
people that don't win!

00:00:04.597 --> 00:00:06.720
If you win, they're
going to talk about you.

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:09.187
You've wasted too much of your life

00:00:09.187 --> 00:00:11.533
trying to change other
people's mind about you.

00:00:11.533 --> 00:00:13.408
Don't tell me that you want something

00:00:13.408 --> 00:00:16.345
if you're not willing to throw

00:00:16.345 --> 00:00:17.656
what you got at it.

00:00:17.656 --> 00:00:18.660
- Hello Believe Nation!

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:19.493
My name is Evan Carmichael.

00:00:19.493 --> 00:00:20.634
My one word is believe,

00:00:20.634 --> 00:00:22.834
and I believe that
entrepreneurs will solve

00:00:22.834 --> 00:00:24.883
all of the world's major problems.

00:00:24.883 --> 00:00:26.841
So to help you on your journey today

00:00:26.841 --> 00:00:28.922
we're going to learn from
pastor and thought leader

00:00:28.922 --> 00:00:30.384
Bishop T.D. Jakes,

00:00:30.384 --> 00:00:32.537
and my take on his top
10 rules for success,

00:00:32.537 --> 00:00:33.756
volume two.

00:00:33.756 --> 00:00:35.726
Rule number 10 is my personal favorite,

00:00:35.726 --> 00:00:37.213
and I'd love to know which one

00:00:37.213 --> 00:00:38.536
you guys like the best.

00:00:38.536 --> 00:00:40.086
And as always, as you're watching,

00:00:40.086 --> 00:00:42.293
if you hear something that
really resonates with you,

00:00:42.293 --> 00:00:43.912
please leave it in the comments below.

00:00:43.912 --> 00:00:45.976
Put quotes around it so
other people can be inspired.

00:00:45.976 --> 00:00:47.650
You might win a prize as well.

00:00:47.650 --> 00:00:49.450
And also when you write it down,

00:00:49.450 --> 00:00:52.576
it's much more likely to
stick for yourself as well.

00:00:52.576 --> 00:00:53.409
Enjoy.

00:00:53.409 --> 00:00:56.281
(airplane soars)

00:00:56.281 --> 00:00:59.364
(instrumental music)

00:01:06.373 --> 00:01:09.336
- Do you have the courage

00:01:09.336 --> 00:01:11.532
to act outwardly

00:01:11.532 --> 00:01:13.876
on what you see inwardly?

00:01:13.876 --> 00:01:15.613
(audience cheers)

00:01:15.613 --> 00:01:18.372
Or will you die a dreamer?

00:01:18.372 --> 00:01:20.749
Will you die on the verge and on the edge

00:01:20.749 --> 00:01:24.416
in the land of could have,
would have, and should have?

00:01:28.572 --> 00:01:32.322
The strong hand rules the roost.

00:01:33.289 --> 00:01:35.136
Do you have the courage?

00:01:35.136 --> 00:01:36.621
I'm going to drop something on you.

00:01:36.621 --> 00:01:39.538
It takes courage to be successful.

00:01:42.565 --> 00:01:46.732
It is far easier not to be successful.

00:01:48.142 --> 00:01:50.376
Misery will always have company.

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:51.482
(audience cheer)

00:01:51.482 --> 00:01:54.863
Success breeds contempt.

00:01:54.863 --> 00:01:58.738
If you don't want to
make waves, be mediocre.

00:01:58.738 --> 00:02:01.342
Be normal and fit in.

00:02:01.342 --> 00:02:03.812
And if you're more concerned about people

00:02:03.812 --> 00:02:05.162
then you are God,

00:02:05.162 --> 00:02:07.964
then neutralize everything He put in you

00:02:07.964 --> 00:02:09.838
just fit in with everybody else.

00:02:09.838 --> 00:02:10.993
Dress like 'em!

00:02:10.993 --> 00:02:11.888
Walk like 'em!

00:02:11.888 --> 00:02:12.816
Act like 'em!

00:02:12.816 --> 00:02:13.813
Eat like 'em!

00:02:13.813 --> 00:02:15.088
Go where they go!

00:02:15.088 --> 00:02:16.188
Think like they think!

00:02:16.188 --> 00:02:17.188
Do what they do!

00:02:17.188 --> 00:02:19.688
And once you've
neutralized your uniqueness

00:02:19.688 --> 00:02:21.265
you don't need courage.

00:02:21.265 --> 00:02:23.413
It takes courage to be different

00:02:23.413 --> 00:02:26.388
It takes courage to go where
you've never gone before.

00:02:26.388 --> 00:02:29.488
For some of you it took courage
to come to this conference.

00:02:29.488 --> 00:02:32.116
It takes courage to get
you outside of the bar.

00:02:32.116 --> 00:02:34.514
It takes courage to be successful!

00:02:34.514 --> 00:02:36.263
It takes courage to win!

00:02:36.263 --> 00:02:38.938
People don't talk about
people that don't win.

00:02:38.938 --> 00:02:41.341
If you win they're
going to talk about you!

00:02:41.341 --> 00:02:44.414
Do you have the courage to stand there,

00:02:44.414 --> 00:02:46.539
though the storms keep raging,

00:02:46.539 --> 00:02:48.539
and the people get to talkin,

00:02:48.539 --> 00:02:50.964
and you stand there and
say, I've come to far

00:02:50.964 --> 00:02:53.048
to turn around!

00:02:53.048 --> 00:02:56.300
Touch your girlfriend and
say, do you have the courage?

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:58.550
- [Audience] Do you have the courage?

00:02:58.550 --> 00:03:02.975
(applause)

00:03:02.975 --> 00:03:05.725
- I'm going to say something to you.

00:03:08.992 --> 00:03:12.574
It takes courage to be exceptional.

00:03:12.574 --> 00:03:14.873
It takes courage to be wise.

00:03:14.873 --> 00:03:17.576
It takes courage to be rich.

00:03:17.576 --> 00:03:20.150
It takes courage to be educated.

00:03:20.150 --> 00:03:22.199
It takes courage to be knowledgeable.

00:03:22.199 --> 00:03:24.474
Because the moment you do,
but you don't talk like,

00:03:24.474 --> 00:03:27.707
Oh, you forgot where you
came from, look at you.

00:03:27.707 --> 00:03:29.275
It takes courage!

00:03:29.275 --> 00:03:30.300
(audience cheers)

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:32.036
And I'm just wondering

00:03:32.036 --> 00:03:34.736
In this weak, watered
down, mediocre society

00:03:34.736 --> 00:03:36.636
that we live in today.

00:03:36.636 --> 00:03:39.862
In this reality TV world we live in today.

00:03:39.862 --> 00:03:42.536
I'm wondering if there's anybody left

00:03:42.536 --> 00:03:43.814
that's got the courage

00:03:43.814 --> 00:03:45.739
to say after all I've been through,

00:03:45.739 --> 00:03:48.363
and all my ancestors have been through,

00:03:48.363 --> 00:03:50.363
and all my parents have been through,

00:03:50.363 --> 00:03:52.112
I didn't come through all of that

00:03:52.112 --> 00:03:54.287
just to fit in with normalcy,

00:03:54.287 --> 00:03:56.995
I have the courage

00:03:56.995 --> 00:03:58.981
to go after my dream!

00:03:58.981 --> 00:04:02.120
To be anxious is to have
anxiety about something

00:04:02.120 --> 00:04:03.894
that hadn't even happened yet.

00:04:03.894 --> 00:04:07.069
Some of you are so worried
about the threat of trouble.

00:04:07.069 --> 00:04:08.075
You're not in trouble

00:04:08.075 --> 00:04:10.495
it's just that trouble has threatened you.

00:04:10.495 --> 00:04:12.645
And the threat of what might happen,

00:04:12.645 --> 00:04:13.622
what could happen,

00:04:13.622 --> 00:04:17.325
(audience cheering)

00:04:17.325 --> 00:04:18.533
it's wearing you down.

00:04:18.533 --> 00:04:20.566
Half of the things that you
though were going to happen

00:04:20.566 --> 00:04:21.843
never did happen.

00:04:21.843 --> 00:04:24.792
But if you allow those
thoughts to dwell in your mind

00:04:24.792 --> 00:04:27.952
it will succeed at
robbing you of your peace,

00:04:27.952 --> 00:04:29.317
robbing you of your joy,

00:04:29.317 --> 00:04:31.044
robbing you of your life,

00:04:31.044 --> 00:04:34.617
just because you thought yourself
into a nervous breakdown.

00:04:34.617 --> 00:04:36.692
You thought yourself into depression.

00:04:36.692 --> 00:04:39.067
You thought yourself into defeatism.

00:04:39.067 --> 00:04:41.318
The mind is a battleground.

00:04:41.318 --> 00:04:44.271
The fight is in your mind.

00:04:44.271 --> 00:04:46.687
So I want to challenge you to waste

00:04:46.687 --> 00:04:47.987
no more effort

00:04:47.987 --> 00:04:50.284
wrestling with other people.

00:04:50.284 --> 00:04:53.323
(audience yells)

00:04:53.323 --> 00:04:54.156
Oh I lost you,

00:04:54.156 --> 00:04:54.989
(audience cheers)

00:04:54.989 --> 00:04:57.064
I lost you, you were doing
real good, I lost you.

00:04:57.064 --> 00:04:59.962
(audience clap and cheer)

00:04:59.962 --> 00:05:03.773
Your destiny, your
future is not predicated

00:05:03.773 --> 00:05:06.669
on the decision of someone else.

00:05:06.669 --> 00:05:07.740
(audience cheers)

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:09.600
You wasted too much of your life

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:13.250
trying to change other
people's mind about you.

00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:14.278
(audience cheers)

00:05:14.278 --> 00:05:17.401
It doesn't matter what
they think about you.

00:05:17.401 --> 00:05:19.798
God is not going to bless
you by their opinion.

00:05:19.798 --> 00:05:23.931
God is going to bless you
by how you see yourself.

00:05:23.931 --> 00:05:26.028
(audience cheers)

00:05:26.028 --> 00:05:28.668
Touch somebody and say I
believe I'm coming out.

00:05:28.668 --> 00:05:30.742
- [Audience] I believe I'm coming out

00:05:30.742 --> 00:05:32.917
- I don't know how long it's goin take!

00:05:32.917 --> 00:05:35.342
I don't know what I'm going
to have to go through!

00:05:35.342 --> 00:05:37.293
I don't know what I'm going
to lose along the way!

00:05:37.293 --> 00:05:40.909
But I still believe that I'm coming out!

00:05:40.909 --> 00:05:43.461
I've been broke, I've
been busted and disgusted

00:05:43.461 --> 00:05:46.459
but I still believe that I'm coming out!

00:05:46.459 --> 00:05:49.533
I'm locked up in prison,
they say I'll never get out,

00:05:49.533 --> 00:05:53.183
But I still believe that I'm coming out!

00:05:53.183 --> 00:05:56.031
I'm coming out, if I don't
have no where to stay!

00:05:56.031 --> 00:05:58.753
I'm coming out if my
husband marry somebody else!

00:05:58.753 --> 00:05:59.586
(audience cheers)

00:05:59.586 --> 00:06:01.211
I'm coming out if I don't have no job!

00:06:01.211 --> 00:06:03.982
I'm coming out, oh, oh!

00:06:03.982 --> 00:06:06.100
The people who've became
the most successful

00:06:06.100 --> 00:06:06.933
in our society,

00:06:06.933 --> 00:06:08.875
are people who broke the rules.

00:06:08.875 --> 00:06:12.500
You know there was no presidents
for 24 hour news cycle

00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:13.953
until Ted Turner did it.

00:06:13.953 --> 00:06:16.150
They're so many people
who got out of the box.

00:06:16.150 --> 00:06:19.275
Look at Apple and the birth
of the whole notion of Apple.

00:06:19.275 --> 00:06:20.978
Or Nike, I talk about in the book,

00:06:20.978 --> 00:06:22.850
and the birthing of their corporation.

00:06:22.850 --> 00:06:24.409
How they did something
with the tennis shoe

00:06:24.409 --> 00:06:25.578
that had never been done before.

00:06:25.578 --> 00:06:29.578
If you only base your
decisions on empirical data,

00:06:29.578 --> 00:06:32.250
you can only repeat what
somebody else already did.

00:06:32.250 --> 00:06:33.779
If you follow your instincts

00:06:33.779 --> 00:06:35.426
and your own God-given creativity,

00:06:35.426 --> 00:06:37.428
we can go where we have not been before.

00:06:37.428 --> 00:06:42.190
Be strong and very courageous.

00:06:42.190 --> 00:06:45.828
Be strong and very courageous.

00:06:45.828 --> 00:06:48.657
Be strong and be of good courage.

00:06:48.657 --> 00:06:53.033
Be strong and possess the land.

00:06:53.033 --> 00:06:55.420
Because God knows

00:06:55.420 --> 00:06:58.454
that for what you're going to do

00:06:58.454 --> 00:07:00.539
It is not by outer strength.

00:07:00.539 --> 00:07:03.372
(audience cheers)

00:07:04.844 --> 00:07:06.938
You understand, you understand.

00:07:06.938 --> 00:07:09.186
Help me preach this
thing this morning, girl.

00:07:09.186 --> 00:07:11.712
It's inner strength.

00:07:11.712 --> 00:07:15.098
So my fourth point is you
got to have inner strength,

00:07:15.098 --> 00:07:15.931
for this fight.

00:07:15.931 --> 00:07:18.223
It's not your outer strength,

00:07:18.223 --> 00:07:19.674
it's not by might

00:07:19.674 --> 00:07:23.591
nor by power, but by My
Spirit, saith the Lord.

00:07:24.673 --> 00:07:27.352
So you got to have that inner, that inner,

00:07:27.352 --> 00:07:31.575
that inner, that gut
strength, that belly strength,

00:07:31.575 --> 00:07:36.149
that devil-defying, come
hell or high water strength.

00:07:36.149 --> 00:07:37.949
That roll me out in front of them

00:07:37.949 --> 00:07:40.074
and I'll preach from a chair strength.

00:07:40.074 --> 00:07:43.451
That tenacity to take a
lickin and keep on tickin.

00:07:43.451 --> 00:07:46.700
That inner strength that
when I can't do as I would

00:07:46.700 --> 00:07:50.174
I'm gon do as I can but
I'm not gon stop doing,

00:07:50.174 --> 00:07:53.757
to the best of my
ability I'm gone stretch!

00:07:55.384 --> 00:07:57.314
Hallelujah!

00:07:57.314 --> 00:07:58.147
Be strong!

00:07:58.147 --> 00:08:00.502
(audience cheers)

00:08:00.502 --> 00:08:01.910
Strong!

00:08:01.910 --> 00:08:03.192
Strong!

00:08:03.192 --> 00:08:04.481
Strong!

00:08:04.481 --> 00:08:05.703
Strong!

00:08:05.703 --> 00:08:08.286
I am afraid that too many times

00:08:09.474 --> 00:08:12.440
we have pent so much focus

00:08:12.440 --> 00:08:15.720
on teaching you to be good seed

00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:17.570
that we haven't taught you,

00:08:17.570 --> 00:08:20.961
the power of good soil.

00:08:20.961 --> 00:08:24.819
And so when we come to soilless issues,

00:08:24.819 --> 00:08:26.986
the seed ignores the soil.

00:08:28.348 --> 00:08:29.920
We flick the channel,

00:08:29.920 --> 00:08:31.894
that has nothing to do with me.

00:08:31.894 --> 00:08:36.319
We close our eyes because
we have been taught to be

00:08:36.319 --> 00:08:38.417
good seed.

00:08:38.417 --> 00:08:41.285
But we have not been taught
to pay attention to soil.

00:08:41.285 --> 00:08:43.069
And yet the Bible is clear,

00:08:43.069 --> 00:08:46.832
Jesus says the sower
went for a sowing seed.

00:08:46.832 --> 00:08:50.098
And some fell by the wayside.

00:08:50.098 --> 00:08:52.822
Some fell amongst rocks,
some fell amongst thorns.

00:08:52.822 --> 00:08:56.747
The whole text is about environment.

00:08:56.747 --> 00:08:59.580
(audience cheers)

00:09:00.538 --> 00:09:03.333
Look at you

00:09:03.333 --> 00:09:07.416
and look at your environment.

00:09:09.575 --> 00:09:12.884
Have you been positioned

00:09:12.884 --> 00:09:16.384
to flourish?

00:09:18.663 --> 00:09:22.155
Positioning has a lot
to do with flourishing.

00:09:22.155 --> 00:09:24.952
To be in an environment, in
a family that supports you,

00:09:24.952 --> 00:09:26.601
my sister and I were
talking the other day.

00:09:26.601 --> 00:09:29.428
I was telling her what
an amazing person she is,

00:09:29.428 --> 00:09:32.628
that all of our lives
together and all the things

00:09:32.628 --> 00:09:33.729
that God did in my life,

00:09:33.729 --> 00:09:36.596
not once in all the
years that I've known her

00:09:36.596 --> 00:09:39.977
and she was there when Momma had me,

00:09:39.977 --> 00:09:42.488
have I ever known her to be jealous of me.

00:09:42.488 --> 00:09:43.385
(audience claps)

00:09:43.385 --> 00:09:46.155
Not once, not ever.

00:09:46.155 --> 00:09:49.721
She has always been my
cheerleader and my greatest fan.

00:09:49.721 --> 00:09:52.567
And she said, how can I be
jealous of you, you're my brother

00:09:52.567 --> 00:09:56.219
I said a lot of people have
siblings that hate them,

00:09:56.219 --> 00:10:00.136
that are jealous of them,
that hope they choke!

00:10:04.302 --> 00:10:08.067
And some of my development
has to be that God planted me

00:10:08.067 --> 00:10:12.199
in an environment of people

00:10:12.199 --> 00:10:14.199
that supported me.

00:10:14.199 --> 00:10:16.048
My brother, my sister,
my mother, my father,

00:10:16.048 --> 00:10:17.948
they all supported me.

00:10:17.948 --> 00:10:21.850
You can have good seed!

00:10:21.850 --> 00:10:25.922
But if you've been in bad soil,

00:10:25.922 --> 00:10:28.272
people who hated you,

00:10:28.272 --> 00:10:30.750
environments that denied you,

00:10:30.750 --> 00:10:33.174
education that underserved you,

00:10:33.174 --> 00:10:35.451
communities that limited you,

00:10:35.451 --> 00:10:38.097
mentalities that poisoned you.

00:10:38.097 --> 00:10:40.930
(audience cheers)

00:10:41.925 --> 00:10:44.123
Do you hear what I'm saying?

00:10:44.123 --> 00:10:48.141
If your soil wasn't right,

00:10:48.141 --> 00:10:49.788
it doesn't mean that you're not right,

00:10:49.788 --> 00:10:52.254
but if your soil wasn't right,

00:10:52.254 --> 00:10:55.402
it's going to affect how
you root and how you grow.

00:10:55.402 --> 00:10:58.053
And you might grow a
little bit the Bible says

00:10:58.053 --> 00:11:01.154
you can grow for a while
but then the thorns

00:11:01.154 --> 00:11:02.653
will choke you out.

00:11:02.653 --> 00:11:05.203
Or the rocks will not have enough soil

00:11:05.203 --> 00:11:07.103
for your roots to grow!

00:11:07.103 --> 00:11:10.391
Are you blaming God

00:11:10.391 --> 00:11:13.779
for something you ought to
be blaming the soil for?

00:11:13.779 --> 00:11:18.526
You cannot take a peach seed

00:11:18.526 --> 00:11:21.833
and plant it in a teaspoon of dirt

00:11:21.833 --> 00:11:23.913
and expect it to grow.

00:11:23.913 --> 00:11:26.120
Though the teaspoon of
the dirt is the same size

00:11:26.120 --> 00:11:28.719
as the peach seed, it will not grow.

00:11:28.719 --> 00:11:31.770
The seed will only grow when it is planted

00:11:31.770 --> 00:11:34.437
in something bigger than itself.

00:11:35.370 --> 00:11:38.497
And I want to know where are
you planted this morning?

00:11:38.497 --> 00:11:41.120
Are you planted in
something bigger than you?

00:11:41.120 --> 00:11:44.703
Or have you always been
planted in teacups?

00:11:45.869 --> 00:11:48.672
Surrounded by little
dirt, little resources,

00:11:48.672 --> 00:11:52.258
small-minded people,
narrow, limited places

00:11:52.258 --> 00:11:55.698
that never let you stretch
to reach your capacity.

00:11:55.698 --> 00:11:59.115
Sometimes you got to go where the corn is.

00:12:00.218 --> 00:12:02.664
- [Charles Payne] You call
comfort in your book a cage.

00:12:02.664 --> 00:12:03.977
- [Bishop T.D. Jakes] Comfort is a cage.

00:12:03.977 --> 00:12:06.327
We use to be pioneers, that's
how this country was settled.

00:12:06.327 --> 00:12:08.706
And we stop pioneering new things.

00:12:08.706 --> 00:12:10.877
We stay where it's comfortable.

00:12:10.877 --> 00:12:11.904
We play where it's safe.

00:12:11.904 --> 00:12:15.453
We don't really get out into
the wild of the possibilities.

00:12:15.453 --> 00:12:17.508
We stay in the confined cage of

00:12:17.508 --> 00:12:21.583
that is tangible and touchable,
9 to 5 and that's it.

00:12:21.583 --> 00:12:23.832
But we need more creativity

00:12:23.832 --> 00:12:25.204
and we need to follow our instincts.

00:12:25.204 --> 00:12:27.703
Now without that you may makes some money

00:12:27.703 --> 00:12:29.256
but you won't find fulfillment.

